# rpmlintrc for the media-preservation mpf package (personal OBS home:
# project). The mpf-check, mpf-cli and mpf-gui subpackages each ship a
# permissions.d profile that grants cap_sys_rawio to their binary
# (/usr/lib64/mpf-{check,cli,gui}/MPF.{Check,CLI,Avalonia}) so vendor SCSI
# passthrough works without sudo — the same capability the Fedora/COPR (%caps)
# and Ubuntu/PPA lanes already ship. rpmlint applies rpmlintrc filters across
# all built subpackages, so this one file covers all three profiles.
#
# openSUSE's rpmlint flags any non-whitelisted permissions.d profile with
# `permissions-file-unauthorized` (Badness 10). That code is a BlockedFilter in
# opensuse.toml: it cannot, by design, be silenced with addFilter (that would
# defeat the security review). Submitting to openSUSE Factory would instead
# require the profiles to be reviewed and whitelisted in the central
# `permissions` package. For this personal repo the capabilities are intentional
# and packager-reviewed, so drop the badness to 0 to keep the rpmlint score
# clean. Verified in a Leap 16.0 chroot: all three caps land (getcap) and the
# profiles parse (permctl).
setBadness("permissions-file-unauthorized", 0)
